--TEST--
A `void` call has no value: at `mixed` it is `E0401`, as a `match` arm `E0868` whether the `match` is a value or a statement, and as a ternary branch `E0718` (`rule:expressions/a-match-has-at-least-one-arm`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Job {
    public static function run(): void {}
    public static function count(): int {
        return 1;
    }
}

mixed $x = Job::run();
int $n = Job::count();
match ($n) { 1 => Job::run(), default => 0 };
mixed $y = match ($n) { 1 => 2, default => Job::run() };
$n > 0 ? Job::run() : Job::run();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `mixed`, found `void`
%A
9 | mixed $x = Job::run();
%A
error[E0868]: this `match` arm calls a function that returns `void`
%A
11 | match ($n) { 1 => Job::run(), default => 0 };
%A
error[E0868]: this `match` arm calls a function that returns `void`
%A
12 | mixed $y = match ($n) { 1 => 2, default => Job::run() };
%A
error[E0718]: a call that returns `void` has no value, so it is not an operand
%A
13 | $n > 0 ? Job::run() : Job::run();
%A
error[E0718]: a call that returns `void` has no value, so it is not an operand
%A
error: aborting due to 5 errors
